    "hardest_step": 2,
    "hardest_step_why": "以-4为例，5%仅±0.2；纵轴每5分一格且无点值标签，精度先卡在步骤2。整页正文虽多，但图表上下文清晰。Step 2 is the hardest because the chart’s values are not printed and must be inferred from a 5-point y-axis grid. Small values such as −4 and −8 have very narrow 5% tolerances (±0.2 and ±0.4), making reliable reading difficult. The additional significance encoding by marker shade and the two-level category axis increase addressing complexity, but the labels and figure context are present and generally associable.",
